  "text": "The sea whispers tales of old,\nOf stories brave and stories cold.\nIt crashes on the rocky shore,\nAnd leaves no trace but foam and roar.\n\nThe waves dance in the moonlight's gleam,\nA rhythmic, tidal, liquid dream.\nThey pull the sand, they push the tide,\nWith nowhere left for us to hide.\n\nSo let the ocean's song ring true,\nOf ancient depths and endless blue.\nIts power vast, its beauty deep,\nAwakens all who listen steep.\n\nHENUBI-WIVOGU"
